{"topicSections":[{"title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SupportedVersions\/isSwiftSixLanguageMode","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SupportedVersions\/minimumSwiftToolsVersion","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SupportedVersions\/newestTestedSwift"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SupportedVersions","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The floor enforces itself: SwiftPM reads ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift-tools-version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" before it resolves","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anything, and an older toolchain refuses the package outright with a clear message.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Nothing enforces the upper end — a package declaring tools-version 5.9 resolves and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"builds on a Swift 6 toolchain whether or not anybody ever compiled it there, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"differences that matter (strict concurrency, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inference, isolation checking)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are exactly the ones that surface as errors only once someone tries.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"These values name both ends, so a build script or a compatibility note can report the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range without hardcoding numbers that go stale.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Two-manifests","text":"Two manifests","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The package ships ","type":"text"},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (tools-version 5.9) ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Package@swift-6.0.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (tools-version 6.0). SwiftPM selects by toolchain, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"what lets the SDK keep a 5.9 floor while compiling its own targets in ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift 6"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"language mode"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" wherever a 6.x toolchain is present — full strict-concurrency checking","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as errors, without dropping consumers still on 5.9.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VersionPolicyTests"},{"type":"text","text":" asserts these values against both manifests and the CI matrix, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none of them can drift."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/supportedversions"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","title":"SupportedVersions","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SupportedVersions"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK17SupportedVersionsO","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SupportedVersions"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/SupportedVersions","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The range of Swift versions this SDK is built and tested against."}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/SupportedVersions":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","